y has been discussed by"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Weinberg, S."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/53072"}},{"reference":{"label":"6","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"112","artid":"669","year":1958,"page_start":"669","journal_title":"Phys.Rev."},"authors":[{"full_name":"Haag, R."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9166"}},{"reference":{"label":"6","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"35","artid":"34","year":1962,"page_start":"34","journal_title":"Helv.Phys.Acta"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Ruelle, D."}]}},{"reference":{"imprint":{"publisher":"Academic"},"label":"6","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"25","artid":"270","year":1960,"page_start":"270","journal_title":"Nuovo Cim."},"misc":["For a discussion in the context of Lagrangian perturbation theory, see the contribution by one of us (S. C.) in IIadrons and Their Interactions, A. Zichichi (eds.) Press inc., New York, 1968)"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Borchers, H.J."}]}},{"reference":{"label":"7","misc":["This decomposition amounts to a particular parametrization of the left cosets G/II by means of the parameters $~. Any other parametrization would give rise to a treatment completely equivalent from the abstract group-theoretic point of view and would furnish equivalent results. However, the particular parametrization we use here is very convenient because of the simple and wellknown properties of exponentials. Alternative parametrizations have been used in concrete applications and can be found, for instance,. in the papers quoted in Ref. 1"]}},{"reference":{"label":"8","misc":["This case has been considered in detail by (private communication)"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Biedenharn, L.C."}]}},{"reference":{"label":"9","misc":["As a special case of this result, we recall that, in nonlinear phenomenological theories, the pion is described as a threedimensional multiplet and it is not necessary to introduce the e 6eld which would be needed to complete the four-dimensional linear representation of SU(2)&(SU{2).This does not mean, however, that one cannot introduce the cr into the theory, if experimental evidence requires one to do so. The 0, being an isoscalar, would be described as an invariant under the full group SU(2) XSV(2). The strength of its couplings to other fields will be unrelated to that of the couplings of the pion to the same Gelds. Nevertheless, invariance under the group imposes well-de6ncd restrictions on the a couplings"]}}],"number_of_pages":9,"referenced_authors_bais":["Steven.Weinberg.1","Julian.Seymour.Schwinger.1","R.Haag.1","Richard.P.Feynman.1","J.A.Cronin.1","H.T.Nieh.3","J.E.Wess.1","B.Zumino.1","B.W.Lee.1","Sidney.R.Coleman.1","C.G.Callan.1"],"legacy_version":"20170208154417.0","legacy_creation_date":"1996-05-15","preprint_date":"1969","author_count":3,"first_author":{"affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/03vek6s52"}],"full_name":"Coleman, Sidney R.","ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE ID","value":"INSPIRE-00145833"},{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"Sidney.R.Coleman.1"}],"last_name":"Coleman","first_name":"Sidney R.","recid":1013257},"control_number":54959,"dois":[{"value":"10.1103/PhysRev.177.2239"}],"earliest_date":"1969","document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Coleman:1969sm"],"abstracts":[{"source":"APS","value":"The general structure of phenomenological Lagrangian theories is investigated, and the possible transformation laws of the phenomenological fields under a group are discussed. The manifold spanned by the phenomenological fields has a special point, called the origin. Allowed changes in the field variables, which do not change the on-shell S matrix, must leave the origin fixed. By a suitable choice of fields, the transformations induced by the group on the manifold of the phenomenological fields can be made to have standard forms, which are described in detail. The mathematical problem is equivalent to that of finding all (nonlinear) realizations of a (compact, connected, semisimple) Lie group which become linear when restricted to a given subgroup. The relation between linear representations and nonlinear realization is discussed. The important special case of the chiral groups SU(2)×SU(2) and SU(3)×SU(3) is considered in detail.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"APS"}}],"refereed":true,"titles":[{"title":"Structure of phenomenological Lagrangians. 1."}],"external_system_identifiers":[{"schema":"OSTI","value":"4812328"},{"schema":"SPIRES","value":"SPIRES-78840"}],"facet_author_name":["981906_Bruno Zumino","983748_Julius Wess","1013257_Sidney Richard Coleman"],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:54959","updated":"2023-03-07T05:18:03.580694"},"curated":true,"journal_title_variants":["Phys. Rev.","Phys.Rev."]},"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/54959?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/54959?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/54959?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/54959?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/54959?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/54959?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A54959"},"updated":"2023-03-07T05:18:03.580694+00:00","created":"1996-05-15T00:00:00+00:00","id":"54959"}],"total":1},"links":{"self":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Coleman%3A1969sm&size=10&page=1","bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Coleman%3A1969sm&size=10&page=1&format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Coleman%3A1969sm&size=10&page=1&format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Coleman%3A1969sm&size=10&page=1&format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Coleman%3A1969sm&size=10&page=1&format=json","json-expanded